 change existing  court precedents  that say appellate courts must defer to  the rulings of judges  who make racially biased comments during  jury selection  all of these things happen in real cases  cited by the new laws  reform alliance policy director erin  haney says one of the new laws  changes the way defendants serve their  sentences  what we found is that there are so many  studies that show  that the best amount of time to be under  supervision in any state  for any offense is actually 18 months or  less  probation is most effective within that  period of time  and when you keep people on probation  for longer than that  what ends up happening is that you see  people going back  into prison for technical violations  which are non-crimes um so this could be  being late to a meeting with your  probation officer  not being able to keep full-time  employment any number of conditions of  probation  so by changing something like the amount  of time that you are sentenced to  probation in california  just from three years to one year for  misdemeanors and from  five years down to two years for  felonies you  actually save over five years 48  000 plus prison admissions just for  technical violations  and 24 000 years of freedom so there  will be people  who would have been locked inside a  prison on technical violations because  they have been sentenced to  three years or five years who will now  be free  and be able to be productive members of  their communities  how hard was it to convince the governor  and the legislature to pass these  reforms  assembly assemblymember comlogger was  just a force of nature  as was assembly member ash kara buffy  wicks  there were just so many people who  worked incredibly incredibly hard to get  these reforms passed governor gavin  newsom has been such a great leader  in criminal justice in the state of  california and so  we owe so much to him he is managing so  many different things and for him to  step  up and be this leader 